26538"}]}],"start":0,"end":517}],"sections":[{"heading":"History","level":2,"wikitext":"Enforcer Titans are standard issue amongst [[Klaus]]' team of [[Suits]]. {{source|Home Turf}} Three were summoned at once in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] in attempt to stop the Huntik team from escaping. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} \n\n[[Rassimov]]'s Suits were also equipped with the Titan. {{Source|Coming of Age}} Several Enforcers were used in the Ethiopian desert to attack the Huntik team. {{Source|The Golden Asp}} Enforcer's lasers were later used to severely damage Dante's house in [[the Professor]]'s organized attack on the Huntik team. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}}","text":"Enforcer Titans are standard issue amongst Klaus' team of Suits. [Home Turf] Three were summoned at once in the Tomb of Nefertiti in attempt to stop the Huntik team from escaping. [The Sceptre Deception]\n\nRassimov's Suits were also equipped with the Titan. [Coming of Age] Several Enforcers were used in the Ethiopian desert to attack the Huntik team. [The Golden Asp] Enforcer's lasers were later used to severely damage Dante's house in the Professor's organized attack on the Huntik team. [The Secret of Two Generations]"},{"heading":"Suit 004's Enforcer","level":3,"wikitext":"This [[Unnamed Suit 004|Suit]] summoned her Enforcer to attack the Huntik team in a burger restaurant. It fought [[Santiago]] before facing off against [[LeBlanche]]'s [[Sentinel]]. {{source|All Work and No Pay}}","text":"This Suit summoned her Enforcer to attack the Huntik team in a burger restaurant. It fought Santiago before facing off against LeBlanche's Sentinel. [All Work and No Pay]"},{"heading":"Hoffman's Enforcer","level":3,"wikitext":"Hoffman's Enforcer accompanied him, [[Wilder]] and his team as they travelled by speedboat to [[:Category:Avalon|Avalon]] He was called back to his [[Amulet]] as they docked on the shore. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}}","text":"Hoffman's Enforcer accompanied him, Wilder and his team as they travelled by speedboat to Avalon He was called back to his Amulet as they docked on the shore. [Knight of the Willblade]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"Enforcer has attack power similar to [[Strix]] but has increased defensive capabilities. These Titans can shoot lasers from one or more of its eyes, this lasers are strong enough to defeat weaker Titans such as [[Feyone]]. {{source|To Be Together}} and and weaken stronger ones like [[Freelancer]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}} Enforcer's claws are razor-sharp like axes however they aren't commonly used in battles.\n\n{{clear}}","text":"Enforcer has attack power similar to Strix but has increased defensive capabilities. These Titans can shoot lasers from one or more of its eyes, this lasers are strong enough to defeat weaker Titans such as Feyone. [To Be Together] and and weaken stronger ones like Freelancer. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs] Enforcer's claws are razor-sharp like axes however they aren't commonly used in battles."},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nEnforcer Amulet.jpg|Enforcer's Amulet\nEnforcer Icon.jpg|Enforcer's Icon\nEnforcer.jpg|Enforcer\n</gallery>","text":"Image caption: Enforcer's Amulet\n\nImage caption: Enforcer's Icon\n\nImage caption: Enforcer"},{"heading":"Trivia","level":2,"wikitext":"* Enforcer's summoning command is \"'''Go get him'''\".","text":"• Enforcer's summoning command is \"Go get him\"."},{"heading":"International Names","level":2,"wikitext":"{{InternationalNamesSmall\n|FR = Enforceur}}\n\n{{SwaraBox}}\n\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Sharpshooter Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]","text":"French: Enforceur"}],"full_text":"Enforcer is a flying, insectoid Swara-Titan possessing six arms. It has three red eyes for its face from which it can shoot laser beams. Enforcer is a weaker cousin of Mindrone and Terrapede, and is used by members of the Organization for ranged and aerial combat.\n\nHistory\n\nEnforcer Titans are standard issue amongst Klaus' team of Suits. [Home Turf] Three were summoned at once in the Tomb of Nefertiti in attempt to stop the Huntik team from escaping. [The Sceptre Deception]\n\nRassimov's Suits were also equipped with the Titan. [Coming of Age] Several Enforcers were used in the Ethiopian desert to attack the Huntik team. [The Golden Asp] Enforcer's lasers were later used to severely damage Dante's house in the Professor's organized attack on the Huntik team. [The Secret of Two Generations]\n\nSuit 004's Enforcer\n\nThis Suit summoned her Enforcer to attack the Huntik team in a burger restaurant. It fought Santiago before facing off against LeBlanche's Sentinel. [All Work and No Pay]\n\nHoffman's Enforcer\n\nHoffman's Enforcer accompanied him, Wilder and his team as they travelled by speedboat to Avalon He was called back to his Amulet as they docked on the shore. [Knight of the Willblade]\n\nAbilities\n\nEnforcer has attack power similar to Strix but has increased defensive capabilities. These Titans can shoot lasers from one or more of its eyes, this lasers are strong enough to defeat weaker Titans such as Feyone. [To Be Together] and and weaken stronger ones like Freelancer. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs] Enforcer's claws are razor-sharp like axes however they aren't commonly used in battles.\n\nGallery\n\nImage caption: Enforcer's Amulet\n\nImage caption: Enforcer's Icon\n\nImage caption: Enforcer\n\nTrivia\n\n• Enforcer's summoning command is \"Go get him\".\n\nInternational Names\n\nFrench: Enforceur","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox titan\n| image      = File:Enforcer.jpg\n| attack     = 2\n| defense    = 2\n| type       = [[Swara-Titan]] Sharpshooter\n| size       = Average\n| ability    = Buzzjump <br> Gatling Eye\n| height     = 6 feet\n| weight     = 190 pounds\n| first      = \"[[Home Turf]]\"\n| users      = [[Alpha]]<br>[[Beta]]<br>[[Hoffman]] <br>[[Suits]]<br> [[Unnamed Suit 004]] <br> [[Unnamed Suit 025]] <br> [[Unnamed Suit 026]] <br> [[Unnamed Suit 027]] <br> [[Unnamed Suit 028]] <br> [[Unnamed Suit 029]]<br>[[Unnamed Suit 054]]\n}}\n'''Enforcer''' is a flying, insectoid [[Swara-Titan]] possessing six arms. It has three red eyes for its face from which it can shoot laser beams. Enforcer is a weaker cousin of [[Mindrone]] and [[Terrapede]], and is used by members of [[the Organization]] for ranged and aerial combat. \n\n== History ==\nEnforcer Titans are standard issue amongst [[Klaus]]' team of [[Suits]]. {{source|Home Turf}} Three were summoned at once in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] in attempt to stop the Huntik team from escaping. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} \n\n[[Rassimov]]'s Suits were also equipped with the Titan. {{Source|Coming of Age}} Several Enforcers were used in the Ethiopian desert to attack the Huntik team. {{Source|The Golden Asp}} Enforcer's lasers were later used to severely damage Dante's house in [[the Professor]]'s organized attack on the Huntik team. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}}\n\n=== Suit 004's Enforcer ===\nThis [[Unnamed Suit 004|Suit]] summoned her Enforcer to attack the Huntik team in a burger restaurant. It fought [[Santiago]] before facing off against [[LeBlanche]]'s [[Sentinel]]. {{source|All Work and No Pay}}\n\n=== Hoffman's Enforcer ===\nHoffman's Enforcer accompanied him, [[Wilder]] and his team as they travelled by speedboat to [[:Category:Avalon|Avalon]] He was called back to his [[Amulet]] as they docked on the shore. {{Source|Knight of the Willblade}}\n\n== Abilities ==\nEnforcer has attack power similar to [[Strix]] but has increased defensive capabilities. These Titans can shoot lasers from one or more of its eyes, this lasers are strong enough to defeat weaker Titans such as [[Feyone]]. {{source|To Be Together}} and and weaken stronger ones like [[Freelancer]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}} Enforcer's claws are razor-sharp like axes however they aren't commonly used in battles.\n\n{{clear}}\n== Gallery ==\n{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nEnforcer Amulet.jpg|Enforcer's Amulet\nEnforcer Icon.jpg|Enforcer's Icon\nEnforcer.jpg|Enforcer\n</gallery>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Enforcer's summoning command is \"'''Go get him'''\".\n\n== International Names ==\n{{InternationalNamesSmall\n|FR = Enforceur}}\n\n{{SwaraBox}}\n\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Sharpshooter Titans]]\n[[Category:Organization Titans]]\n[[Category:Average Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 1 Titans]]","categories":["Average Titans","Organization Titans","Season 1 Titans","Sharpshooter Titans","Swara-Titans","Titans"],"links":[{"target_id":"huntik:page:2842","status":"resolved","target_title":"Swara-Titan","label":"Swara-Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Swara-Titan","href":"#/categories?name=Swara-Titans"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:3228","status":"resolved","target_title":"Home Turf","label":"Home Turf","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Home_Turf","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A3228"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:26527","status":"resolved","target_title":"Alpha","label":"Alpha","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Alpha","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26527"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:26528","status":"resolved","target_title":"Beta","label":"Beta","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Beta","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A26528"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4577","status":"resolved","target_title":"Hoffman","label":"Hoffman","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Hoffman","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4577"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2050","status":"resolved","target_title":"Suits","label":"Suits","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Suits","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2050"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:17523","status":"resolved","target_title":"Unnamed Suit 004","label":"Unnamed Suit 0